    "summary": "Both findings addressed. (1) handoffBranchName now refuses a branch name in which ANY slash-separated component ends in .lock (or starts with a dot), as git does, not just a name that ends in .lock: 'foo.lock/{id}', 'x/y.lock/{id}', '{id}.lock' and '{id}/.hidden' are refused; the pure branch-name test lists them, and the parkPlan test's invalid-pattern loop now includes 'foo.lock/{id}' and 'x/y.lock/{id}' and expects ok:false with the branch reason. (2) Scope: I reverted src/daemon/steps/workflow-step/park-offer.ts to exactly its t5 content (git diff against t5's commit is empty), so this task no longer touches the sibling. parkPlan therefore has its own non-exported copy of the 'is this run for this unit' check, and the duplication is logged as open issue S6-1 in docs/plans/s6-open-issues.md (to be merged once the Story is built). The earlier t6 fixes stand: the planner reads the tracker context with createIssue false so it never creates an issue, and the branch is validated before any git command. config/github.ts's resolveBranchPattern remains, as the only way to read the repo's branchPattern. Pure, park-plan and park-offer tests pass; tsc clean.",
